        "pr_number": 14757,
        "pr_file": "Solutions/SecurityScorecard Cybersecurity Ratings/SolutionMetadata.json",
        "discussion_id": "3654631921",
        "commented_code": "@@ -1,11 +1,11 @@\n {\n-\t\"publisherId\": \"SecurityScorecard\",\n-\t\"offerId\": \"SecurityScorecard\",\n+\t\"publisherId\": \"securityscorecard\",\n+\t\"offerId\": \"securityscorecard\",",
        "comment_created_at": "2026-07-28T06:34:50+00:00",
        "comment_author": "sigmabaryon",
        "comment_body": "**`domains`** - `\"Security\"` is not a valid value: it is absent from `.script/SolutionValidations/ValidDomainsVerticals.json`, and no other solution in the repo uses it. `\"Security - Others\"` is the valid equivalent (29 solutions use it). `SolutionValidations` passes with this change.\r\n\r\n**`publisherId` / `offerId`** - lowercased to match the documented rule (`^[a-z][a-z0-9]{0,49}$` in `solution-metadata.instructions.md`); 487 of 515 solutions are all-lowercase and none use mixed case. Flagging it explicitly, though, because it does change `variables('solutionId')` from `SecurityScorecard.SecurityScorecard` to `securityscorecard.securityscorecard`, which feeds `_solutioncontentProductId` through a case-sensitive `uniqueString()`. If Content Hub needs the published identity preserved for the 2.0.0 -> 3.0.0 upgrade path, we are happy to revert this one - please confirm which you would prefer.\r\n",
        "pr_file_module": null
      }
    ]
  },
